{{#is_alert}}
## P1 · API availability — error budget burn (fast)
**WHAT:** Error budget for API availability is being consumed 14.4× faster than sustainable, confirmed over 1h and still true over the last 5m.
**WHERE:** {{value}} · env `prod` · region `global`
**SERVICE:** `api-services` (api / slo, tier0)
**BUSINESS IMPACT:** Customer-facing objective at risk. At the current rate the 30d budget is exhausted well before the window ends.
**WHY IT TRIGGERED:** Multi-window burn rate: the long window (1h) proves the burn is sustained rather than a spike, and the short window (5m) means it is still happening now. Both must be true, which is what makes burn-rate alerting both fast and quiet.
**OWNER:** application-development · support 24x7 · this pages the on-call rotation
**DO THIS NEXT:** Identify the largest contributor to the budget burn (service, endpoint, dependency), then follow the error-budget runbook. If the burn is a known incident, attach this alert to the existing incident rather than opening a new one.
**RUNBOOK:** https://github.com/droderiquesit/enterprise-observability/blob/main/platform/runbooks/slo-error-budget-burn.md
**AUTOMATED DIAGNOSTICS:** workflow `auto-major-incident` has run; its output is attached to this event.
**RELATED EVENTS:** correlated on `api-services.prod.api-services` — deployments, infrastructure changes and platform events from the last 30 minutes are attached as context.
**SLO / ERROR BUDGET:** `slo-api-availability` · this condition consumes error budget
{{/is_alert}}
{{#is_warning}}
